    "faq_XyKTzC": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_row_XdLKBG": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q1. Can you add Google Cloud or Vertex AI to our existing AWS or Alibaba Cloud environment?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We can assess an integration alongside your existing environment without requiring a complete migration. Connectivity, data access, and rollout plans depend on your architecture. We plan testing and rollback procedures to manage production risk.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_ckALeW": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q2 How do you address 429 errors and production capacity constraints?",
            "answer": "<p>We identify whether errors relate to quotas, shared capacity, or application traffic patterns. Depending on the workload, options may include capacity planning, request pacing, retries with backoff, suitable endpoint selection, or reserved throughput. Availability and terms depend on the selected service. No architecture can promise that every future 429 error will be eliminated.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_8DWdMn": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q3. How are projects priced?",
            "answer": "<p>Scope, milestones, deliverables, and commercial terms are agreed before delivery. Cloud consumption and third-party charges are identified separately where applicable. Changes follow an agreed scope-change process. Any provider credits depend on eligibility and approval.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_6Vcq7e": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q4. Can our engineers maintain the solution after handover?",
            "answer": "<p>We design the agreed solution for your team's operating needs and provide relevant documentation, code, and training. The level of ongoing expertise and support depends on the system's complexity and your internal capabilities.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_idcK38": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q5. How do you reduce AI inference costs?",
            "answer": "<p>We assess model choice, request size, routing, batching where supported, and caching for reusable inputs. Decisions are validated against output quality and performance requirements. Savings depend on the starting workload and are measured rather than guaranteed.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_mtDEQH": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q6. Who owns the infrastructure and code?",
            "answer": "<p>Ownership and licensing are defined in the contract. Customer-specific deliverables can be deployed to customer-controlled accounts and repositories, while third-party services and reusable components retain their applicable terms. Access is transferred through secure account and IAM processes.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_TfzdMb": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q7. How long does delivery take?",
            "answer": "<p>Timing depends on integrations, data readiness, security reviews, and capacity availability. We agree a schedule after discovery. A focused proof of concept has a different scope from a production rollout. Individual case timelines are examples, not standard commitments.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_CGMX33": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q8. How do you handle data privacy and compliance?",
            "answer": "<p>We assess data flows, regions, permissions, retention, and encryption requirements with your team. Provider terms and model-specific data handling are reviewed for the selected configuration. Technical controls can support compliance, but a cloud deployment alone does not establish GDPR compliance or SOC 2 attestation.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
